  "findings": [
    "ADP1-ADP3: exact finite class order gamma*t*z*k and compact infinity give compact quotient; the actual quotient measure yields a positive definite form on continuous functions. Evaluation bounds Hom_{G_infty}(S,A)^K for every open finite subgroup, and the precise finite-orbit/fixed-dimension hypotheses of PKT5-PKT6 are satisfied.",
    "ADP4-ADP5: the finite-dimensional unitary matrix-algebra argument makes each S tensor U irreducible; evaluation is nonzero and injective. The resulting algebraic sum of actual function subspaces admits globally equivariant coordinate projections, finite on each prescribed finite-dimensional subspace. No Hilbert closure or multiplicity-free claim is used.",
    "ADP6: the exact away/ell projection is surjective already on the finite factor and its kernel is the infinite factor; opposite split coordinates determine the missing finite entries. The original polynomial infinity action is trivial on finite-only elements and continuous at infinity, with literal rational compatibility through the specified basis E.",
    "ADP7: right translation by x has functional precomposition by R(x^-1) in the correct order R((g*x)^-1)=R(x^-1)R(g^-1). Rational equivariance gives left invariance; finite stabilizers and finite dual dimension give the exact smoothness and infinity-finiteness clauses; continuity uses the actual product topology, never continuity of iota.",
    "ADP8-ADP9: biduality gives Psi(g*z)=R(z^-1)Psi(g), so R(g)Psi(g) descends on precisely the p-fibers. This gives the required rational coefficient function for every source Phi, preserving E and all maps. Direct comparison with PlaceBetween.formU confirms all five clauses, including the arbitrary J constrained pointwise to equal the original p.",
    "ADP10: the added all-depth principal-congruence argument proves openness of I1(b) for every original b, including the exact b+1 indexing. The finite intersection of that condition, original auxiliary/away levels and the type-kernel condition yields one neighborhood before every coordinate and functional. The matrix-valued level equation then gives coordinate smoothness.",
    "ADP11-ADP12: each globally equivariant projection commutes with finite translation lifts and scalar matrix mixing. Inverse scalarization preserves the original Big coefficient equations. The finite sum lands in the literal YOf=Big intersect span of all scalarizations lying in sigma, proving full decompU."
  ],
  "corrections_resolved": [
    "Inserted explicit arbitrary-depth I1(b) openness, since inherited FNL7 alone states depth zero."
  ],
  "boundary_preserved": [
    "FV and FNL inherited geometric and quotient-measure inputs",
    "No arithmetic decoration of an automorphic constituent",
    "PartAltAlt, AutomorphicHeckeSet and partU_alt/partX_alt remain separate",
    "No arithmetic nonvanishing, full same-ideal Hida endpoint, RH or GRH conclusion",
    "No Lean replay"
  ]
